  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Many times people are operating in large groups in invite/friends worlds. However, it is not always a good idea to move at once to other worlds. This can be for reasons of available player slots, physical size, performance issues, or even accessibility issues such as excessive motion, noise, flashing lights, etc.\n\nIf the world host had the option to drop a portal to a specific instance that lasted much longer, this could set up a whole range of new possibilities. An ad-hoc \"lobby\" could be set up that could have one or several portals available that people could join an already running instance with others. This would let people freely move between games, special maps, small instances etc. A busy game or club world could have a chill-down space. The portal could be dropped at the end of a puzzle for a post-game meet-up space. I think that in the broader sense, this would also improve the since of \"place\" in VRChat in general. \n\nReturn portals would be a nice feature, but even just a 'return to last world' or similar button somewhere would be sufficient.",
